  "slug": "scalable-commodity-1353",
  "summary": "Spatial, single-nucleus, and imaging readouts are now coupled to interpretable models and genetic or mechanistic validation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is resolving biological signal by region, cell context, or genetic background and interrogating it with learned models. In Alzheimer's disease, ADVISE disentangles Braak-stage signatures from snRNA-seq and prioritizes ROBO2, validated by CRISPRa, while ADInteractome extracts gene interactions from neural network internal states. ATLAS profiles 40M cells across mouse brains to compare cell-type distributions by genetic background. A head MRI network localizes calvarial bone marrow to estimate adiposity, linking it to heritability, 41 loci and genetic correlations. Adjacent tools address data quality and pathway inference: ComBat-based batch correction of 508 Answer ALS samples, and NEPTUNE's pathway mapping of neuronal death markers. The newer element is coupling resolved readouts to genetic or mechanistic validation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-05"
}
